{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Within three days.</b> Why did Joseph not give a longer time in interpreting the chief cupbearer's dream — only three days? Because he saw that the entire dream concerned something urgent, as it is said: ״והיא כפרחת עלתה נצה הבשילו אשכלותיה״ (and it budded, blossomed, its clusters ripened). And along with the interpretation of this one, he likewise interpreted that of the chief baker." "<b>And he shall restore you.</b> The vav with patach, and the he with hateph-patach."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:06.857213964Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}